# Testing

The project uses Maven, JUnit Jupiter, Mockito, and Spring Boot Test. Follow the current tests under `src/test/java/com/github/farzan6118/petclinic/` and test dependencies in `pom.xml`.

## Current test layout

- Most tests are focused service tests using `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)`, `@Mock`, and `@InjectMocks`.
- Existing service tests cover owner, pet, species, medical-record, vet, vet-availability, duration-template, and visit behavior.
- `PetClinicApplicationTests` is a `@SpringBootTest` context-load test. The normal application profile uses local PostgreSQL configuration, so a full test run may need a reachable/configured PostgreSQL instance.
- There is no configured Testcontainers SQL Server setup, Failsafe integration-test phase, or established `*IT` suite in this repository. Do not write instructions or tests assuming those exist.

## What to test

- For business-rule changes, add or update focused service tests for success, validation/missing-resource cases, status transitions, and relevant conflicts.
- Mock the service's own repositories and external/service dependencies, following adjacent tests. Verify meaningful state, returned values, and important collaborator calls.
- For scheduling changes, cover the affected availability, vet/pet/room overlap, clinic-hours, lock-aware repository call, and notification behavior as appropriate to the change.
- For HTTP binding/status/serialization behavior, use an appropriate Spring web test if the requirement needs it. Do not substitute a mocked-controller unit test for service behavior, and do not assume a database-container harness exists.
- Avoid tests that only restate Bean Validation annotations or call a JPA repository method in isolation.

## Commands

Run focused tests with the Maven wrapper from the repository root, for example `mvnw.cmd -Dtest=OwnerServiceImplTest test` on Windows. Run the full suite with `mvnw.cmd test` when the local database/profile prerequisites are available. Report an environment/database limitation as such; do not hide it by changing test configuration or substituting H2.

Do not add dependencies, alter the database engine, or create a new integration-test framework as part of an unrelated feature.
